# Line-ending policy for files whose exact bytes matter.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Windows default, so without these rules a checkout
# rewrites these files to CRLF.

# The dependency patch is applied by pnpm against LF package sources. A CRLF
# copy fails to apply ("patch does not apply"), which would silently drop the
# v4 rules and leave the pre-write guard advisory.
patches/*.patch text eol=lf

# Generated, byte-compared artifacts. The generators emit LF on every platform
# (scripts/generate-dynamic.mjs and scripts/build-client.mjs normalise), and CI
# asserts the committed copies are not stale — so a CRLF checkout would make
# `pnpm build` dirty them on Windows for no reason.
lib/client.bundle.js text eol=lf
lib/dynamic-host.js text eol=lf
lib/dynamic-client.js text eol=lf
